  "scope": "Document public API identifiers compared against source tokens; shared-document scope reviewed; C++ snippets syntax-checked in their documented context. Syntax checking does not prove all prose or mathematical contracts.",
  "findings": [
    "BinaryTrie and CompressedBinaryTrie previously embedded one shared guide containing the other class and normal-only implementation details. Dedicated source-scoped guides now distinguish types, reserve, ownership, capacity and examples.",
    "SPFA previously embedded BellmanFord-only usage example; BellmanFord page also listed SPFA API not included in its source. Dedicated source-scoped guides now call the correct function.",
    "HLD deliberately needs a user-selected range structure; documentation now states before the first example that Fenwick Tree is a separate source. Noncommutative example uses prose-defined concat/empty_word and the separately included Segment Tree.",
    "Topological.cpp and Topological_sort.cpp have identical implementations; their shared guide is applicable to both.",
    "No other missing public type/function was found by the identifier check; conceptual potentials, callback parameter names and external comparison types are not claims of supplied APIs."
